Chapter: ShiftNegativeCount

  cites Foreword chapter Console

 COMPILER-158: a negative shift count traps (#UD) instead of shifting by its
 low six bits. The line before the shift prints; nothing after it does.

Section: Entry

  shl : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  shl (v) (n) = bit-shl v n

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "before the negative count"
    print-line-uni ("shl 1 -1 " & show (shl 1 (0 - 1)))
    print-line-uni "after the negative count"
  end
